the dungeon. The bounty for B to be used as a potential dungeon boss became extremely high since Carl was so successful in the dungeon. So, Adette arranges to get her. Adette then surprises Carl and Donut with B on an 
episode of her show. We left B heading towards the center system as a citizen of the syndicate. Throughout the book, it is revealed that Carl had an abusive father whom he has to confront in a part of a boss challenge 
in the dungeon. When Carl was 15, his mother attempted a murder-suicide on his father, successfully killing herself but unsuccessfully killing Carl's father. Although it's not specifically revealed in which way Carl's 
mother died, he associates the sound of running water with her death. Carl also finds out that he has a half-brother Asher who B hid from his knowledge before the dungeon. Oh, yeah. And he also now has a pet tummy acre 
named Sir Rendelgor and a wife, Princess Shandra, Donut's lawyer. We don't really know anything about that yet, though. At the end of book 7, Carl is level 81. He chose the primal race and the compensated anarchist 
class, which he upgraded on level six to the agent provocateur class. Some important equipment and items he has. First, the Ring of Divine Suffering. Okay, he doesn't actually have this anymore, but as it was a big plot 
point, I feel like we should mention it. This ring allowed him to mark people for death and gain perks when they were killed, with the caveat that you cannot heal until the mark is killed. It was an incredibly dangerous 
ring that both Donut and Mordecai specifically continually wanted Carl to give up. He finally does at the end of the seventh book. Carl's Sleeveless Jacket. Carl has a jacket in which he can add patches to give him 
benefits. He has several patches that give a variety of skills and boosts, but I'll mention two with story implication here. The Scavenger's Daughter patch is a divine item, meaning it can gain benefits or debuffs based 
on whether a specific deity is present. It also allows Carl to store up soul energy to fill a meter that once filled can be released in a single strong melee attack. This may corrupt Carl over time as in the words of 
the AI, "Warning, you know how asbestos is really bad for you? Like, it doesn't hurt you immediately, but it builds up in your lungs and eventually screws you over? Actually, you know what? Just ignore this warning. 
Forget I said anything. Carrying corrupted essence around on your back builds character. You already have a ring that's doing much worse to you anyway." This patch also has the bone key benefit, giving Carl a one-time 
use open any lock benefit. However, using this key benefit will destroy the patch and the jacket it's attached to. It will also take a bone from the user's body based on how difficult the lock was to open. The harder 
the lock, the bigger the bone taken. The Reaper Spider Minion patch gives Carl access to the Midnight Market. He also has the Dungeon Anarchist Cookbook, the book that appears worthless to everyone else but is actually 
a book with notes from previous crawlers to help future crawlers destroy the crawl. It was created by the system AI during the 15th season of the Dungeon Crawler world. Carl's currently writing the 25th edition. The 
cookbook will get its own entry in this recap later. Carl's Doomsday Scenario. A giant explosive created at the end of book 2. It is unstable and has a 1-second timer if removed from Carl's inventory. It's just 
chilling, so probably good to remember that he has this. The Eye of the Bedlam Bride tattoo. She Maria tattoos her third eye onto Carl's chest with special ink at the end of book 6. With the help of Hipponzi, She 
Maria's husband, they contain her during book 7. Because of that, the implications of what this tattoo can still do moving forward are unclear. And finally, Embers. Carl worshipped Embers to save themselves during the 
events of the Gate of the Feral Gods. Since then, he has been tasked with discovering who killed Embers's son and to kill Embers's brother Helak before the 12th floor. Currently, where we are in the quest, Carl needs to 
get a memorial crystal that Prepotente currently has, and he also has to kill 100 worshippers of Helak before the 12th floor. He is still working on clues to discover who killed his son. Next up is the character I 
