consistently treated Kadia terribly. Kadia has the race Doppelganger and class Monster Truck Driver. Her race allows her to shapeshift into whatever form she'd like to take, which Carl helps her hone and she uses to 
great effect later in the dungeon. Throughout the novels, we learn that Kadia desperately wanted to be a mother but was unable to conceive. She was in the process of adopting a child, Annie, when she discovered her 
partner, Finnur, was having an affair with a student. She reported him, and he retaliated by reporting her former drug addiction history to the adoption agency, making the adoption fall through. Annie was suffering from 
brain cancer and would pass away before the collapse without being adopted. Although Kadia kills Eva on the fifth floor after Eva forces the Crown of Sepsis [ __ ] on her, Eva was also responsible for Kadia relapsing 
by leaving her a present of Blitz Sticks for her to find. Kadia has to deal with his addiction through the next few floors. Kadia's current status is ineligible and out of the dungeon. In order to help her and Donut 
escape the ninth floor alive, she used the Orchid of Ophelia. She had three choices: a constitution boost, to become a celestial attendant and return to the dungeon on the 12th floor, or to leave the dungeon, have her 
race permanently changed back to her birth race, and become pregnant. She chose the third option and was exited from the game and transported to an on-Earth facility for other pregnant or too young participants for the 
crawl. Louis becomes the father of Kadia's child. On becoming human again, everyone in the party realizes that Kadia has been hiding what she's lost. Her entire right arm is missing to the shoulder. Her left leg was 
gone, as well as her right leg up to the knee. She's also missing an ear. She stated her goal was to help the children that are still in trouble on Earth, and this would help her get to them. Samantha. Samantha is the 
minor deity Samayth, currently stuck in the decapitated head of a like-a-love doll. She has a daughter named Mrs. Gazi, a sentient sand creature whom Samantha believes is currently dead. Samantha is currently trying to 
regain a body. It also seemed that she is slowly getting stronger even in her head-only form. Mordecai. Mordecai is currently Carl and Donut's manager. He was a former crawler in the dungeon who took an exit deal on the 
11th floor. Originally a sky fae, he took the changeling race in the dungeon, and so now appears as a random race every new floor. Mordecai is particularly adept in potion making. Mordecai is currently on his last crawl 
in his indentured ship, which has lasted centuries because a rule was changed shortly after he left the dungeon that only allowed him to participate in crawls run by the Born Corporation, which obviously wasn't every 
crawl. Mordecai holds a lot of anger and resentment towards his former manager during the crawl, Odette, and his team member, Chaco, because they formed a plan in the dungeon that resulted in the death of his brother 
after he had decided to sacrifice himself instead for the team. This was done because Odette selfishly needed Mordecai to reach the 11th floor so that her indentured ship would end early and she would have enough money 
to sustain herself outside the crawl. As mentioned previously, Mordecai will be incredibly angry if he finds out he was manipulated into becoming a manager, especially by Odette. Odette Odette is a famous former crawler 
and the host of the dungeon show Dungeon Crawler After Hours with Odette. In the crawl, she lost her legs on the 11th floor and now uses a flying disc to get around. Her show persona has giant crab legs attached to her 
torso. Odette has helped the Royal Court on multiple occasions, but has also acted a little shady on multiple occasions as well. Ultimately, her allegiances are still in question. Mordecai obviously has a history with 
her and often warns about how selfish she is. It seems that Odette is still very concerned for Mordecai and may be attempting to still help him. Odette plans on participating in the ascendancy games to claim the 
celestial throne by sponsoring Nekabit. Hi Zev. Zev initially starts as Carl and Donut's representative for the Born Corporation, but has since been moved to their social media manager. Zev is a Quaten, a small humanoid 
