her multiple player killer skulls. Ellie Gibbons was a former patient of the Metalark Elder Care facility and was confined to a wheelchair and had dementia. Upon reaching the third floor, she took the race Frost Maiden, 
which helped restore her memory and mobility. Finally, Brandon and Chris, who are brothers and also worked at Metalark. Brandon was friendly with the Royal Court and dies on the third floor after failing to get to a 
stairwell. He asked Carl to find Chris, who left the party, and to apologize for him and tell him that he loves his brother. Chris chose the Igneus race and now resembles a lava rock monster. His change in personality 
was because Maggie Mae had infiltrated his mind on floor three. Carl is able to rip her out of Chris and save him from her influence. Everyone from the Metalark team are trusted friends of the Royal Court. Daniel 
Bautista. Bautista is a friend of the Royal Court and is in a romantic relationship with Kadia. Bautista chose the Tigrin race and so looks like a humanoid tiger. Lena, Lejun, and Jeong. Carl and Donut helped save the 
party of Lena, Lejun, and Jeong on the second floor, causing Lejun to be a particular friend of the Royal Court. Lejun and Lena are siblings while Jeong is their friend and in love with Lena, although Lejun doesn't know 
it. On the eighth floor, when She Maria takes over Carl, she ends up stabbing out and eating one of Lejun's eyes, giving Carl one of Lejun's abilities. Later, he is rewarded a robotic eye from the dungeon. At the end of 
floor nine, Lejun sacrifices himself to save Donut and Lena stabs out one of her own eyes and replaces it with Lejun's artificial eye. Lena is currently in trouble because on the seventh floor, she used the Ring of 
Divine Suffering to mark a large group of people, but two got away. She currently cannot heal. Florin Florin is a close ally of the Royal Court. He met up with a crawler in the dungeon named Ifechi and bonded quickly 
with her. Due to some trickery on Lucia Mar's part, Florin ends up killing Ifechi while trying to kill Lucia. He is almost ready to completely give up when he hears how Carl and Donut have worked selflessly to save 
other crawlers and credits them with his ability to keep going. Despite initially wanting to kill Lucia Mar himself in revenge, he is the person to first discover that more is going on with her than meets the eye and 
