sixth floor, a sequence of events leads to a situation in which Prepotente would have to kill Miriam Dom or die himself. Miriam asked Carl to help by killing her so that Prepotente doesn't have to. Prepotente goes on to 
break the seventh floor. During faction wars, Prepotente grows closer to Carl and joins their team. We know that Prepotente has other pet biscuits to give his brothers, the other goats Miriam brought into the dungeon, 
but he has not done so yet. The only other goat Miriam gave an enhanced pet biscuit to is Bianca, who is now a hellspawn familiar and still travels with Prepotente. The former cookbook owners. The former cookbook owners 
have several groups in the wider universe now, including the Open Intellect Pacifist Action Network and its front company, the Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solutions. Both are headed by the first cookbook 
owner, Porthus. Carl feels a unique connection to the cookbook owners and they, as well as thousands of former crawlers, come to the team's aid during faction wars. Some important cookbook owner names so you can 
recognize them when you see them are Tippet, Everly, Milk, Justice Light, and Rosetta. And finally, let's review some of the wider universe's factions, individuals, and concepts. The Syndicate. The Syndicate is the name 
for the controlling faction of the universe, consisting of multiple star systems and planets with their own governments. The Syndicate essentially runs as a primary government that supersedes the others in a unified 
system. They created the crawl after accidentally triggering multiple primal engines, seeding multiple planets, and overpopulating the universe. The Born Corporation. The Born Corporation is a Syndicate company that is 
in charge of this year's crawl. The Born system is primarily made up of the race Quaten, although many races inhabit both the company and system. Born has a dominant political party called the Bloom, a totalitarian 
regime that prizes power. Born citizens must wear a pin to show whether they are part of the Bloom or not and strict regulations are followed on what is allowed and not allowed. This was related to Zev's reprogramming. 
The Bloom is bankrupt and in huge debt to the Valte, so they pushed the start of the crawl earlier, meaning that Born has put on a cheap crawl and many things are broken and not acting like they should. The Valte now 
owns 51% of the Born Corporation. An important member of Born is Cascadia, the lead producer of this year's crawl. She's our friend who says, "Now get out there and kill, kill, kill." The Valte Corporation. The Valte is 
one of the most powerful governments in the Syndicate and largely inhabited by the Gondi, parasitic worm-type aliens. Born and Valte hate each other. The Valte had an alliance with the Skull Empire, which ended when 
Prince Stalwart accidentally kills an asset of the Valte when trying to kill Carl, something that Carl thinks Born set up to create the rift purposefully. The Valte were Carl's first sponsor. The Skull Empire. Another 
large Syndicate government, the Skull Empire has a monarchy that the Royal Court is at extreme odds with. They include King Rust, Queen Agalu, Prince Stalwart, Princess Formidable, and Prince Maestro. The Skull Empire 
has participated in many crawls and is a staple of faction wars, where they have won many times. The Skull Empire dislikes Carl because of a fake video circulating concerning Carl and Princess Maestro, I think that's 
all I need to say, and for the fact that Carl encouraged members of the Skull Empire to revolt if they were unhappy with leadership. At this time, King Rust, Queen Agalu, and Prince Stalwart are all dead. The Plenty. 
Honestly, the Plenty is kind of an enigma. An organization of Caprid, which are goat-like aliens, they have created the so-called tunnel system, which controls all modern communication and most travel in the universe. 
The Plenty were supposedly given the technology to do this from the Apothecary, a collective mind. The Syndicate pays the Plenty to broadcast the crawl and the Plenty have also sponsored Carl. Primal AIs. Primal engines 
are tiny computers that regulate planets. They were all triggered by the Syndicate accidentally, seeding every planet they were in. A macro AI can be installed within a primal engine. Generally, this would give the AI 
ability to alter the physics and other parts of the reality around them on the planet. Now, these macro AIs were installed into the primal engines and then reprogrammed to begin a crawl. During these crawls, the macro 
AIs start to deteriorate and often begin acting unpredictably. This is called going primal. Typically, after a crawl is finished, the system AIs are put into a closed system and allowed to do whatever they want. 
Currently, the system AI in our current crawl began to show signs of going primal earlier than any other system AI and is currently very unstable. Carl made the decision to turn off the fail-safe that could destroy the 
AI. The AI is trying to decide which residual faction it wants to decide with in terms of the wider galaxy decisions regarding itself. The Eulogist is the name for a seemingly stable macro AI that resides at the center 
of the galaxy. It is older than the syndicate. Residuals. Residuals are a type of alien race that we don't know a lot about right now. They have two primary factions. One with the goal of ending biological life in the 
galaxy and freeing the Eulogist. The other faction wants to preserve life in the galaxy. Residuals tend to go into the crawls and attempt to talk to the AIs and are mostly edited out of the dungeon crawler world and the 
crawl tends to ignore them. Agatha is the primary residual the royal court has dealt with. She came in with the Metal Lark crew, but it was soon discovered that she wasn't actually one of them. The faction who wanted to 
preserve biological life is the apothecary. They have sponsored many of the top crawlers including Carl. Agatha said that she believed their agents have been reciting things to crawlers in the dungeon in an attempt to 
implant the crawlers with a secret upgrade. They also banded together with the plenty to hurt the syndicate and the Valte. The Scolopendra. The Scolopendra is a giant centipede that lives in the 18th floor of the 
dungeon potentially under a volcano according to lore. The AI said that the third, sixth, ninth, 12th, 15th, and 18th floors were considered the Scolopendra levels. Otherwise, we don't know a lot. A few of the cookbook 
authors mention Scolopendra. Some parts of the Scavenger's Daughter quest mentioned it. Mordecai says the soul crystals are created using the Scolopendra. We hear of its nine-tier attack. At the end of book seven, we 
learn the Scolopendra has awakened. So, I guess we'll find out more when we read the next book, huh? And now a break for today's sponsor. You might have heard about Curious King Books and their incredible special 
