the dungeon. Carl gets to visit a prize carousel and the person running the carousel is Chaco. Mordecai attempts to attack him in a safe room and is put in a seven-day timeout. Carl selects the Dungeon Anarchist 
Cookbook as his prize. While at first it seems useless, Carl realizes it contains information from dozens of former crawlers. Carl and Donut go to the Desperado Club and hire Bomo and Sledge as private security. Carl 
chats with Ellie and Imani and talks about Chris. Suddenly, he sees that Donut's cockroach skull is triggered. He turns to see her bloody and that she's killed the crawler that attacked her gaining a player killer 
skull. They meet the assistant manager Astrid and negotiate to have Bomo and Sledgy as their guards at the club moving forward. The team derails a train and learns from an engineer several things about the path to the 
stairwells, none of which are easy. And unfortunately, the primary one involves using a hat you received at the start of the level that many people have already sold. The team received their first sponsors. Carl is 
sponsored by the Valte, Donut is sponsored by Princess Donadia, and Katia is sponsored by Princess Formidable. Carl receives a neural enhancer that allows him to access information on portals. The team finds out that 
there is a drug ring happening between mobs and trains and when they don't get their drugs, they morph into stronger monsters. Through Carl's guidance and assistance, Katia practiced making unusual forms with her 
doppelganger ability. They also find out that Quan CH is derailing trains and stranding crawlers. The team meets multiple NPCs like Brandy the engineer and Madison. Through these interactions, they learn that many NPCs 
memories are completely fake or that they reset each time they are reused. And some of these NPCs, through these interactions, become aware of their situation. These interactions lay a framework for how Carl will treat 
NPCs on future floors. Carl meets Frank Q in the Desperado Club. Frank gives Carl the Ring of Divine Suffering and explains what happened. They were forcing their daughter Yvette to use it as she wouldn't kill anyone. 
They'd marked Carl for death, but then he got away meaning Yvette could not heal. She got injured and was in so much pain that Maggie killed her to relieve her suffering. Frank and Maggie split up shortly after and 
Maggie is bent on revenge on Carl. After Carl leaves, Frank is killed by Chris. Heckla, Eva, and other Brynhild's daughters enter their personal space on the invitation of Katia. They ask for help rescuing 1,000 
stranded crawlers, including Lee Joon and Lee Na. Heckla comes up with the idea to have Katia clear the track by sticking herself in front of the train. During the ride, Donut sees Heckla shoot Katia with invisible 
arrows due to her sunglasses. A fight ensues while Katia is confused. Eventually, Eva begins to goad Katia and while Katia tries to kill Eva, she accidentally kills Heckla instead, earning a player killer skull and a 
huge bounty. Carl is able to collect a bunch of hats for the trapped crawlers. Zev warns Carl and Donut that Loida will take over as their representative and that private chats will become public. Donut and Carl have to 
kill an NPC, Crawler Gary, multiple times to collect his hands in order to stage the rescue operation. The rescue plan is only a partial success and they have to come up with a new plan to save those that are still left 
behind. Carl attempts to summon the god Groll to deal with the station mimic, but it goes wrong and he's sucked into the portal as well. It's then revealed that Groll is sponsored by Prince Maestro. Groll ends up 
killing the mimic and Carl nearly escapes death when his friends come to the rescue. They use the nightmare to ascend the stairwell with Fire Brandy and another NPC offering to sacrifice their lives to help. Book four, 
The Gate of the Pharaoh Gods. Welcome to floor five. It's the bubble floor. This floor separates crawlers into different bubbles in which each has four quadrants, sea, land, tomb, and air. Each quadrant has a castle 
which contains a stairwell. If all the castles have fallen, then the bubble pops. Otherwise, you may not leave or enter other bubbles until those conditions have been met. Carl, Donut, and Katia begin in an air 
quadrant. No other crawlers they know are in their bubble. They meet Firus and Louie for the first time, drunkards who are not very adept. Louie attaches himself to a changeling prostitute named Juicebox. Mordecai lets 
Donut know that she can tell which people are changelings by using her sunglasses. The recap shows the showdown between Lucia Mar, Ifechi, and Floren. A plan regarding taking their castle in their quadrant goes awry 
when a key person is killed by other crawlers from a different quadrant. The team receives new sponsors. Carl from Open Intel Pacific Action Network, Donut from Verilex Real Pet Companions, and Katia from Squim 
Conglomerate. Carl receives Tourmaline Root from the Pacifist Network and another neural enhancement from the Balte. They are notified that Chris has liberated the castle in the water quadrant and Carl and Imani discuss 
Chris's change in personality since changing races. Because of their failed plan, Juicebox and other changeling NPCs are in danger. Carl allows them to shelter in their safe room and Juicebox expresses the desire to 
make it to the hunting grounds on the sixth floor. The team fights a boss, Ruckus, and devises a plan to trick a negotiator so that the town is not bombed. During the fight with Ruckus, Carl learns about a device hidden 
in the tomb quadrant, The Gate of the Pharaoh Gods. This device has three parts and when put together, the user can travel from one place to any other. If used in this way, a random Pharaoh God is also summoned. Zev 
returns as their social media manager, but is acting very strange, like she has been brainwashed. Chris appears and talks to Carl, acting strange as well, while Katia receives an emergency benefactor box. Carl realizes 
that Maggie May is inhabiting and controlling Chris and that she is sponsored by Maestro and Stalwart. Donut acts suddenly to stop Carl from having to kill Chris to kill Maggie, delaying the fight till another time. 
Carl and Donut are able to liberate their floating castle, clearing their quadrant, and gaining a piece of the Gate of the Pharaoh Gods. While on a show promoting a robot toy in Donut's likeness for her sponsor, Carl 
rigs the robot to explode, killing Loida. They are immediately pulled away to speak to Oren, a syndicate liaison. They learn 15 admins have been killed already on this season, a disastrously high number. They can't 
prove it was their fault, so they are let go, but discover that they've been gone from the dungeon for a full five days. Katia has grown significantly in this time, holding down the fort for all the crawlers while Donut 
and Carl are gone. They work to liberate the land quadrant by defeating Gazi, the mad sand mage. In the process, they meet Samantha and also get another part of the Gate of the Pharaoh Gods, a map and other vital 
information. They make a plan to shut off a pump in the water quadrant so they can drain the Necropolis. They meet Britney and Vadam and hire Samantha as a trainer so she can come into their safe room. While under the 
water, they have a difficult boss fight. Vadam attempts to escape while leaving the others stranded, but ultimately dies in the attempt. Carl finds the last piece of the Gate of the Pharaoh Gods and uses it to transport 
himself, Katia, and Tran back to town, in the process releasing a Pharaoh God. Carl also receives a reward notifying him that he was sued again, but he won. Sued for his potential use of the Gate of the Pharaoh God. As 
a reward, he receives pictures of all the plaintiffs' mothers. Due to their use of the gate, the god Embers is wreaking havoc looking for his son, Puppy, Orthrus. A group quest is initiated to keep Orthrus safe, who is 
currently stuck inside their bubble since they haven't popped it yet. Once that quest is completed, they get another one to reunite Orthrus and Embers. Quincey H attempts to sabotage the mission and kill Carl. Carl 
worships Embers and throws a celestial grenade to summon Embers to their location, allowing him to reunite with Orthrus and leave. Carl chops off Quincey H's arm before he escapes. Because Carl now worships Embers, he 
has two quests, to find out how he killed his son and to kill Halic, his brother. Carl makes it known that he's going to use the Gate of the Pharaoh God in a specific way that allows him to summon a Pharaoh God into the 
ninth floor, Faction Wars, in order to disrupt things there. Part of the plan involves sending Juicebox there and she makes Carl promise to see the rest of the changelings safely from each floor to the next. While 
waiting to put the plan into action, he confronts Chris and Maggie May again, succeeding in killing Maggie and saving Chris. Katia says she's going her own way on the next floor to save the rest of the daughters from 
Eva. Carl and Katia enact the real plan, which they were actually hiding, which ends up filling Loroco's with water and bombs, killing NPCs and making it harder for the sponsors to prepare for Faction Wars and allowing 
them to also keep the Gate of the Pharaoh Gods. Borant is furious. In the epilogue, we see Gravy Boat and it's also revealed that B is still alive. She is taken to safety on Odette's orders. Book five, The Butcher's 
Masquerade. Welcome to floor six. It's the hunting grounds. Tourists from outside the dungeon have been leveling up to fight against the crawlers. This year, to get more participants, they are allowing registration up 
to the very last minute. Carl's have 30 hours before hunters are released on the floor. This floor also require Carl to make good on his contract to continue the Vengeance of the Daughter program. We begin this book 
with a little over 85,000 crawlers left. The book starts in Oren's office. Carl asks for a lawyer, causing Quasar to appear. In the end, Carl gives up the Gate of the Pharaoh Gods until the ninth floor and in exchange 
gets four mercenaries, Bomo and Sledgy, along with Clayton and Very Solon, as well as spells that can replicate two of the gate's abilities, teleport to stairwell and a spell that allows you to transfer an entire 
settlement to a deeper floor. It's revealed later that the plan is to use that spell to transport a city of changelings to the ninth floor. Donut takes the legendary Diva class, which allows her to sing for buffs to the 
party. Unfortunately, the singing has to be on key and Donut just isn't very good. Carl has Bomo use the teleport to stairwell spell to teleport him and Donut directly into the hunter city before the hunters are 
released. They wreak havoc on the town with bombs and Carl uses the Ring of Divine Suffering to target hunters, despite Donut and Mordecai's growing concerns about him using the ring. Eventually, Carl gets incredibly 
injured and is rescued by Miriam Dom and Prepotente. It's revealed that Miriam Dom is now a vampire. It is announced that a party will be thrown at the end of the floor for the top 50 crawlers. Donut gets credit for 
killing a mayor of a town and ends up mayor herself as per floor rules. The town has been beset by attacks from dinosaurs. [ __ ] runs off into the forest after acting strangely and is found surrounded by small 
dinosaurs. [ __ ] ends up mating with Kiwi, the pack leader, much to Donut's chagrin. The hunters are now released on the floor. Carl and Donut meet up with Signet to continue the storyline. Carl kills a hunter from 
The Dream, a group that has promised vengeance on Louie because he made a comment about the leader of The Dream's mother when Carl got her picture last floor. He loots an arrow that inflicts double gonorrhea, a weapon 
The Dream plans to use on Louie. For the record, I had to look up how to spell gonorrhea and so my Google history is shot. Both The Hive and The Skull Empire have claimed Carl as their kill. Samantha wants to join them 
on their quest because she believes Signet can help her get a body. Carl and Donut receive a new sponsor, The Apothecary. They go on a Dutch show where they find out B is alive and must confront her on air. A 
planet-wide message announces that The Born Corporation is now independent from the Born government and that the Balte have a 51% share in the corporation. Carl sees that Donut has been involved in arranging this, but 
it is too dangerous to discuss how with her. Carl and Donut are warned that the masquerade is likely to have a boss meant to kill most of the top crawlers. Carl and Donut help complete part one of the Vengeance of the 
Daughter quest by taking on Fort Freedom. The next part of the quest requires them to kill Queen Imogene, who will be at The Butcher's Masquerade. They run into Big Tina, the dinosaur that was previously a child ursine 
and transformed during her recital. They receive a quest to either kill Big Tina or help her get what she wants, which they assume is to help her perform and finish her recital. Kiwi is Big Tina's mother. Carl and Donut 
enter a new town and they realize Lucia Mar is the mayor right before Carl is pulled away to go to CrawlCon. While there, he meets a member of his sponsor, The Apothecary, and also meets the mother of two hunters, one 
of whom he has killed and one who is still alive, Fra. Donut warns him that Lucia Mar has set up a trap for his return and that she's angry because Donut managed to kill one of her dogs. Carl manages to avoid the trap, 
killing multiple hunters in the process. He ends up shooting Fra with the arrow of double gonorrhea. Carl goes to his final CrawlCon event. At the event, Carl's new sponsor is revealed since the Balte can no longer 
sponsor him. It's revealed to be The Plenty. Carl attacks another crawler at the event. On return, Carl and Donut get a message from Miriam Dom requesting their help. During a fight, Prepotente's Ring of Divine 
Suffering accidentally marked her so that he can no longer heal while she survives. She asks Carl to kill her, but Carl refuses. Instead, they wait with her until the sun rises. Her dying cures everyone she inflicted 
with vampirism. Prepotente awakes, distraught. Donut speculates that The Plenty set up this event in order for Miriam to die. The team continues to fight and eventually have an interaction with Queen Imogene's familiar 
and it's Ferdinand. A new rule is added to the dungeon, a blood bar that is filled from killing enemies to stop people from being able to hide out in safe rooms. Carl's sponsor, The Open Intel Pacific Action Network, 
warns Carl that the mother of Fra will sponsor the god Diwata. Carl and Donut break into the hunter floor of the Desperado Club to tell the changelings where they need to be during the masquerade for their plan to 
succeed. Dewata enters the realm and marks Carl for death, but does not immediately hunt him. The group suspects she is off to kill Vrah. The group's goals for the parties are to complete the Tina quest, kill Eva, send 
the changelings to the ninth floor, kill Lucia Mar, and kill all the hunters. Queen Imogen appears and as they are warned earlier, she is someone from Earth. It's that she's twin sister. Queen Imogen informs them that 
the party is under a peace seal and breaking it will cause you to be fed into the nothing. [ __ ] performs at the pet show under Donut's guidance. Donut is able to charm Ferdinand to work for their team. Samantha 
turns off the limitations for the crawlers at the party and turns them back on for the hunters. However, elsewhere, Carl's plan is falling apart. Big Tina begins her performance on stage. However, this ends up not 
completing her quest because what she really wants is her mother back, not to finish the recital. Signet dies to break the peace, causing the protections to fall and an all-out war to ensue. In the fight, [ __ ] and 
Kiwi kill Vrah. Donut is able to turn Kiwi back into an Ursine and Big Tina recognizes her, completing the quest. The sledge is able to complete the spell all the changelings to the ninth floor. The final hunters are 
eliminated. Prepotente kills Queen Imogen, completing the vengeance of the daughter quest. Katie kills Eva, but not before Eva can place the crown of the Sepsis [ __ ] on her head. In the aftermath, it is revealed 
that Carl and Donut worked with the Princess Posse and Princess Donadia to secure them a place in faction wars as an official team. Carl encourages Watches to turn off safety protocols for the ninth floor. At the end of 
this novel, we see everyone teleported to the seventh floor where Prepotente proceeds to immediately break it, sending everyone immediately to the eighth floor. Book six, The Eye of the Bedlam Bride. It's floor eight, 
the card game floor, which I guess a lot of people don't like, but I do. Not that you care about that. The floor is designed like Earth with Earth references, no matter how incorrect, and Donut and Carl begin in Cuba. 
Before that though, we start by learning what happened between Mordecai and Odette on this season, which I've already talked about earlier. But basically, Odette arranges to kill Mordecai's brother so that she can 
escape her indentured ship. Another detail here though, indirectly, the reason this plan had to be carried out was because Juan Xin Gen reneged on their deal. This will come back later, so just remember that. Back in 
the present, Carl and Donut began to collect their first cards. They run into crawlers Pazlo, Anton Lopez, and Sister Inez. They team up to collect more cards and start the Chowder War quest, which requires them to 
choose a side between the monk seals and the land craps. You know the quest I'm talking about. Don't make me go into it. Samantha informs the group that while out exploring, she's been eaten by She Maria, or the Bedlam 
Bride. She requires rescue. Carl and Donut, along with their new companions, fight in a corrupted town and receive a quest to repair a shrine. Carl and Donut have to go on a show for Carl's sponsor, the Open Intellect 
Pacifist Network, and he realizes the host is one of the cookbook authors. She tries to pass on information to him in code, but their new liaison from the Plenty suspects cheating and puts a stop to it. However, not 
before Donut catches a clue that they should go to Miami for phase two. Back in the dungeon, they go to complete the shrine quest when suddenly multiple competing deities appear demanding their shrines be fixed. And 
yet, they are only allowed to fix one shrine. Katie informs Carl that unless Simaya's shrine is fixed, they won't be able to solve the dual crown of the Sepsis [ __ ] problem. Carl manages to fix her shrine, but 
contracts slug pox. This is a nasty disease in which boils erupt all over Carl's body and upon popping, produce a slugalow. Each boil and as such slug gets larger and more dangerous as they continue. During the 
resulting chaos from the gods whose shrines weren't fixed, Paz and Anton die, but not before Paz warns Carl and Donut that Sister Inez was a murderer before the crawl and has a special power in the dungeon that makes 
people want to protect her and exposure makes the effect stronger. Alethea, the goddess they need to help with Katie, appears and is sponsored by Juan Told you she'd come back. She gives Carl a spider quest as a cover 
to help them with the crown, but tells Carl not to tell anyone about their deal, including Donut and their other party members. She wants Carl to have Odette as their adjunct for faction wars. Katie gets the prize, the 
Orchid of Alethea's grace, which allows her one of three possible boons, two of which will remove her from the ninth floor. >> [snorts] >> Either she can move to the 12th floor or she become pregnant and thus have to 
leave the dungeon. In order to get the boon, she has one more quest to achieve, killing Astrid, the assistant manager of the Desperado Club. While Carl is in Club Vanquisher to fix his slug pox, the AI gives him a weird 
foot massage and gives him hints for his quest with Empress. Carl gets a floor boon from Empress and is seemingly healed. While attending their first faction wars planning meeting, Juicebox appears disguised as the 
mother Louis said was hot and kills the representative from the dream. The AI won't let them retaliate since she's an NPC. Juicebox asks Carl to create an action item so that the NPCs can have their own faction during 
faction wars. Carl and Katie collect information on how to kill Astrid by visiting the Guild of Suffering, run by the Night Worm in the Desperado Club. The Night Worm is Astrid's husband and he has ordered her death. 
Then, Carl and Donut go to meet up with Samantha who claims She Maria can give her a new body. Carl makes a deal with She Maria, after seeing through her act, that he is allowed to turn her into a card in exchange for 
bringing her to the ninth floor. An update to the floor mechanics is announced that means squads have to find keys and makes it highly likely that squads will have to fight each other decks of the floor, setting up 
crawler on crawler violence. Carl and Donut find out that Katie has relapse and will be out of commission for a while, putting her assassination mission in danger. Donut gets a new sponsor when Empress Donadia drops 
her, the Long Haul Biological Waste Management Solution. She is not pleased about this. The plan to kill Astrid goes a bit awry due to Samantha's antics, but ultimately they accomplish their goal. They discover that 
Damascus Steel and Anaconda, two of the Desperado Club strippers, were Astrid and the Night Worm's children. They demand Carl hire the rest of the dancers from the Penis Parade as their mercenaries to keep them safe now 
that Astrid can't. And they go on a quest to avenge their mother by killing their father. On Odette's show once more, the royal court learns Empress Donadia tried to betray them by introducing action items to eject the 
Princess Posse from faction wars. Odette announces she's sponsoring a deity for Ascension Wars, meaning she can't be their adjunct and the Princess Posse gets Baroness Victory as their adjunct instead, who has ties to 
the School Empire. Alethea tells Carl she'll still help even though Odette isn't their adjunct. Carl and Donut go to fight bosses for their keys and during a scene leading up to the final boss fight, Carl realizes he 
has a half-brother, Asher. Initially, the final fight was supposed to be against Carl's dad, but the AI changes its mind and the final boss is a hydra made up of Carl's former boss, Asher, Asher's mom, Bee's mother, a 
cat show judge, Carl's former friend, Carl's landlord, a former co-worker, and a cat that's Donut's cousin. She Maria helps with the fight, but also does something unknown to Carl when he looks into her eye. Orin tells 
Carl that the AI this season has gone rogue, but has accepted a deal. The faction war teams tried abdicate, but the AI doesn't allow them to. Carl receives a box from the Open Pacifist Network that tells him to visit a 
homeless shelter. During his visit, he meets Goff, a residual that begins to tell him information before Carl's pulled out. Orin informs him that this was a trick designed to force Orin to take Carl out of the dungeon 
in hopes it would anger the AI enough to kill everyone or cause someone to pull the failsafe, destroying the AI and the planet. Pulling Carl out was one of the things Orin pre-negotiated with the AI to avoid these 
scenarios. Back in Cuba for phase three, there are several squads without a key, including Imani and Surendagore's teams. They make a plan to fight Sister Inez for her key to give Imani. We also find out Carl made a 
secret plan earlier in Club Vanquisher and begins by locking the strippers inside a room in the safe room. Carl and Donut find out they failed the Chowder quest and due to other circumstances, combined with all the 
death in the Chowder War, a demon eviction event begins. Quan Chi manages to steal both keys on the floor and runs for an exit. They chase him and Carl plans on using his bone key still to exit the floor while he takes 
back Quan's two keys to give to Imani and Surendagore. They kill Quan Chi, taking both keys. Due to time constraints, Surendagore sacrifices herself so that both Imani and Carl can use the keys. Should I feel bad that I 
haven't mentioned Ren before this when she's been in several books and now she's sacrificed herself for the team? Maybe, but also no regrets because her parts just weren't that important. Sorry. Oh, yeah. And this is 
where Carl gets his meatball pet. The stairwells begin to be compromised and beyond that, Sister Inez is blocking one of the exits they need. Prepotente and Carl come up with a plan to get crawlers without keys to the 
next floor. We find out Lucia Mar helped Katie, Ellie, and Lena with a trick so that they could join Carl's team. Due to the demon eviction event, a lot of souls are needed for the demons to get back and so Carl reveals 
that he infected the strippers with the slug pox and trapped them in the room so that slugalows would constantly be generated. They let them out to help act as souls for the demons. Then multiple gods get teleported in 
and it's like an entire thing, but honestly, you don't really need to know the entire fight beat by beat. And like, I'm not going to talk about that one scene. If you want to read it, just go reread chapter 68. The 
important bit is at the end of all this chaos, Donut tries to combine the She Maria and Alpha Carl cards, but She Maria kills the Alpha Carl card and combines with the real Carl instead, angry that he was trying to 
betray their deal. She Maria gains access to all of Carl's inventory and controlling his movements wreaks havoc. While controlling Carl's body, she injures Katie and [ __ ] and stabs out Lejun's eye and eats it. She 
then tattoos the Eye of the Bedlam Bride on Carl, joining herself to him and giving him some of Lejun's powers. Oh, and during this, all of Carl's hair burns off. At the end of all of that, one of their plans does 
succeed, allowing crawlers to get pulled into a portal spell that's about to go off. And if they position themselves under the stairwells, they can be pulled to the next floor instead, rescuing stranded crawlers. In the 
end, only 5,000 crawlers died on this floor, meaning 33,804 crawlers made it to floor nine. A couple of emergency action items are pulled through for faction wars. Safety protections are now removed for faction sponsors 
and the NPC team is approved. In this epilogue is where we learn a lot about Agatha and the residuals and importantly, find out that the syndicate was considering pulling the failsafe, the thing that will destroy the 
entire solar system, but instead put mercenaries into the dungeon to join faction wars in an attempt to kill all the crawlers and just end the crawl early. We also see Donut's sponsors, Long Haul Waste Management, 
coming to Earth in a ship. It's carrying 50,000 former crawlers to join faction Wars and help the Princess Posse. Book seven, This Inevitable Ruin. Welcome to Faction Wars and the floor where Carl and Donut will have to 
kill the entire Blood Sultanate or else because of the Crown of the Sepsis War. We start this book with a flashback showing that when Carl met with the Residual last floor, he actually received a neural enhancer that 
gave him access to the failsafe. Later in the book, we will find out that Carl freed the AI and made the failsafe non-functional. Back in the wars, the Princess Posse and the NPC team, Team Retribution, join together 
against an alliance of all the other factions. Carl takes a hair potion and now has long hair. Yes, I'm keeping this in the recap. It's important. Juicebox wants to solidify their partnership through marrying Louie and 
Louie seems reluctant although goes through with the first part of the wedding ceremony. Ferdinand shares the Warlord interface for the NPC team. Carl and Donut find out that 50,000 former crawlers are here to help and 
gets emotional at meeting so many cookbook authors. Kiwi is very pregnant with Mango's baby. Carl discovers that She Maria has been consistently trying over and only one of his skills has stopped it. Mordecai begins 
working on a solution to stop this and help Caddie's drug addiction. The treatment will cause Caddie to face her worst memory and Carl to enter She Maria's memory. Carl and Caddie touch while taking the potion causing 
the memories to intertwine instead of stay separate. Carl wakes 11 hours later to discover that it worked and She Maria is contained and Caddie is treated. However, during the treatment, two faction teams had cheated 
using outside information in an attempt to have She Maria kill the entire Princess Posse. The plan backfired causing She Maria instead to wreak havoc and kill the entire Lemex auction base. They are punished for 
cheating. Ferdinand gets approval for an action item to have a feed blackout to stop future outside help and the ceasefire ends early. The Princess Posse begins fighting and kills Donadia and takes control of her 
faction's territory. More fighting ensues with several factions continuing to gain up against the Princess Posse. At one point, they enter parlay with King Rust of the Skull Empire. He reveals that Princess Formidable 
is heading towards where the failsafe is to physically trigger it destroying the rogue AI and the entire planet. He asked Carl to send her message to stop her. Rosetta kills Rust. Carl gets a second ring of divine 
suffering and gives it to Lena. More teams fall and Carl is transferred to a meeting with Oren. The AI appears as an avatar and tells Oren he's upset that he tried to kill him. Says he knows the failsafe doesn't work 
anymore and shows his power by instantly teleporting Formidable to their location and then to the Earth's surface. The AI also discusses which Residual faction decide with. At a Warlord Council, they learn that another 
system AI has gone dark and no one knows if anyone in the system is okay. Carl finds a way to close another outsider information loophole and also discovers that Prepatente has likely killed most of the Blood Sultanate 
as they were the ones involved in Miriam Dom's death. Prepatente joins the Princess Posse in order to be able to work together to fully destroy the Naga. They begin the next phase of attack. Samantha, Prepatente, Lena, 
LeJune and Caddie attack the hidden Naga in Club W Anguisher summoning multiple gods and complete their quest to kill the Blood Sultanate. We see a scene with a former crawler and Juicebox. He reveals that he knows the 
changeling's real purpose to touch as many gods as possible so that they can turn into them. He offers to keep it a secret in exchange for her keeping secret the trap he's building with the gate of the feral gods. 
Agatha enters Faction Wars as a warlord for the War Mage Rebellion. The final phase of Faction Wars begins in which only one team can survive. This puts the Princess Posse and the NPC team in a little bit of a pickle. 
While trying to stop the War Mages from winning, the Royal Court ends up in a tussle with Lucia. Her dog, Gustavo III, is killed and Lucia says, "Now it's too late. Now the Eulogist has another ally in the dungeon and 
now you can't kill me. Not unless you want all the children of Earth to die." LeJune dies to save Donut. During the fight, the god Ares is summoned and gives Carl important information on the War Mages and also 
mysteriously says that Carl is already married. Juicebox manages to save Louie from a tight situation but does so by possessing him and realizes that although she truly loves him, Louie does not love her. Kiwi gives 
birth. The rest of the factions are defeated leaving only the Princess Posse and Team Retribution left. Embrus enters the dungeon saying he will destroy floor nine in just over an hour whether or not he gets the 
information he wants. Lena has used her ring to mark multiple people but a couple of them get away meaning that she won't be able to heal. This finally convinces Carl to give up his ring of divine suffering. Sledgey 
uses his transportation spell to take the entire NPC team to the 12th floor meaning the Princess Posse is the winner. Using specific spells, Donut ends up killing Alethea's host, Want Sing, who had planned to kill 
Odette. Caddie choose to get pregnant and leave the dungeon as her boon. Louie will be the father as Bautista is not an Earth race and cannot be chosen. Some suspect that there is subtext here that implies Caddie really 
wanted Carl as the father but as he is a primal, he is not considered human anymore either. However, I'll leave that up for you to determine as the reader. The team enters the stairwell. We get some reveals at the end. 
The former crawler Justice Light triggers his trap killing himself and causing the nothing to drain into the Shoal, the Hall of Ascension C and then Scolopendra's lair. Scolopendra is awoken. In the epilogue, the Open 
Intellect Action Network plans to move openly against the Syndicate. Carl gets 10th floor deal options which he chooses not to take. He also finds out his new wife is Donut's new lawyer, Princess Chandra. And that 
concludes the summary of the first seven books in Dungeon Crawler Carl. I hope this video was useful for you and I am so excited to read book eight. If you found this video helpful and you like videos like this or other 
DCC videos, please like and subscribe. That is the best way to support what I do here. And as always, if you want to see what I'm currently reading and other nerdy rants, you can check me out on Instagram at 
bookborn.reviews. I'll see you next time. Bye.